            <ArticleTitle>Imaging of coronary artery calcification. Its importance in assessing atherosclerotic disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-72, v</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery calcification is a marker for atherosclerotic disease. The calcifications frequently occur early in the disease process and often before the development of luminal narrowing or cardiac events. Electron beam CT has a high accuracy in detecting calcifications, and thus has prognostic value in predicting luminal narrowing and future cardiac events.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
